jwselect: preperiod selection and covariance-weighted moment adjustment

Research design and method
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source estimator                      | matrix supplied
Independent units                     |       500
Treatment cohorts                     |         2
Target post-treatment cells           |         7
Eligible over-identifying preperiods  |         3
--------------------------------------+---------------------------------------
Baseline                              | Cohort-specific (g-1)
Allowed anticipation (delta)          |         0
Period spacing (gap)                  |         1
Selection method                      | Manually specified preperiods
Candidate preperiod sets              | Not searched (manual selection)
Aggregation                           | Uniform weights across cohorts
Covariance                            | supplied
Inference                             | Normal; fixed restrictions
Post-treatment window                 | All available post-treatment periods
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Preperiod counts are cohort-period pairs, excluding maintained baselines.
Each cohort effect averages its included post-treatment cells equally.

